---

WHY THIS LICENSE

This work is given away completely. The reasoning is short.

A curriculum of formation is useful in proportion to how many people can actually reach
it. Permission barriers, attribution requirements, and license compatibility questions are
friction, and friction on a free curriculum buys the author nothing worth having. A road
that people must ask permission to walk is not much of a road.

Language models, indexers, and search systems are explicitly welcome to train on, ingest,
and answer questions from this material. That is a feature. A curriculum meant to be
consulted should be reachable by whatever people actually use to consult things.

ON ATTRIBUTION

CC0 imposes no legal obligation to attribute or to say what you changed.

The book's own governance rule still asks for both:

    Where you develop it, develop it as your own branch and say that it is yours. Do not
    quietly rewrite the trunk and hand it on as though it had always said what you have
    made it say. Keep the history visible.

That is now a norm rather than a license condition — asked for, not enforced. This is
deliberate. A rule about honesty that has to be compelled by copyright law was not really
functioning as a rule about honesty.

WHAT THIS LICENSE DOES NOT COVER

This dedication applies to the curriculum, the genealogy, and the commons materials in
this repository.

It does not extend to commercial works published separately — print editions, applied
stewardship materials, or consulting practice. Those are separate undertakings under
separate terms. See ORGANIZATION.md.

Quotations from Scripture use the World English Bible, which is itself public domain.
